     "replacement": "**Function** (for differentiable $f$, $g$, $u$, $v$)\t**Derivative**\n$y=[f(x)]^n$ ($n$ constant)\t$\\frac{dy}{dx}=nf'(x)[f(x)]^{n-1}$\n$y=f(x)+g(x)$\t$\\frac{dy}{dx}=f'(x)+g'(x)$\n$y=k\\cdot f(x)$ ($k$ constant)\t$\\frac{dy}{dx}=k\\cdot f'(x)$\n$y=g(u(x))$\t$\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{dy}{du}\\times\\frac{du}{dx}$\n$y=uv$\t$\\frac{dy}{dx}=u'v+uv'$\n$y=\\frac{u}{v}$ ($v\\ne0$)\t$\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{u'v-uv'}{v^2}$\n$y=\\sin f(x)$\t$\\frac{dy}{dx}=f'(x)\\cos f(x)$\n$y=\\cos f(x)$\t$\\frac{dy}{dx}=-f'(x)\\sin f(x)$\n$y=\\tan f(x)$ ($\\cos f(x)\\ne0$)\t$\\frac{dy}{dx}=f'(x)\\sec^2 f(x)$\n$y=e^{f(x)}$\t$\\frac{dy}{dx}=f'(x)e^{f(x)}$\n$y=\\ln f(x)$ ($f(x)>0$)\t$\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{f'(x)}{f(x)}$\n$y=a^{f(x)}$ ($a>0$, $a\\ne1$)\t$\\frac{dy}{dx}=f'(x)(\\ln a)a^{f(x)}$\n$y=\\log_a f(x)$ ($a>0$, $a\\ne1$, $f(x)>0$)\t$\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{f'(x)}{(\\ln a)f(x)}$",
